Z||000000||mikemrq||08-10-2001||05:28 PM||||my '86 fiero v6 4sp, I had a worn clutch replaced. When i picked it up at the shop the clutch grabbed as soon as it left the floor(new clutch felt great) but after a week later, the clutch grabs about half way out. Took it back to the shop, and they said it is fine, the hydrolic clutch will find it's own adjustment-nothing wrong with it.    Is this true???||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||08-10-2001||06:01 PM||||I'd say you should count your blessings. A lot of Fiero owners would kill to get the clutch to grab halfway up. That's actually about where it's supposed to engage. It sounds like it may have worked some air out on it's own.<P>A weak pressure plate is about the only bad thing I can think of that would make a hydraulic clutch engage higher. As long it doesn't appear to be slipping once it's all the way out, I wouldn't worry about it.<P>||||reg||1
